  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Essential Life-Saving Assistance to Crisis-Affected Populations during and after Emergencies in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The armed conflict between the Sudanese Armed Forces (SAF) and the Rapid Support Forces (RSF) that erupted on 15 April 2023 in Khartoum, Darfur, Kordofans and other states of Sudan has internally displaced more than six million people1 and affected millions more across the country. In light of the current context of protection needs, food insecurity, and access to basic goods and services, needs remain critical. This reinforces the urgent need of support through providing emergency relief supplies (shelter, non-food items, and hygiene kits), to reduce the vulnerabilities of displaced and host populations, and help build their immediate resilience capacities to withstand these risks.Through this project, IOM is addressing critical humanitarian needs and contribute to building community resilience through providing emergency shelter (ES) materials, non-food items (NFI), and family hygiene kits to crisis-affected communities in the Darfur states, that include internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host community members in vulnerable situations. IOM plans to distribute relief items through its implementing partners (IPs), who have local presence in the target states and localities, under its common pipeline system.</narrative>
  </description>
